    "title": "1967 Shelby Cobra 427 from The Gumball Rally Movie",
    "summary": "This 1967 Shelby Cobra is one of approximately 260 street-specification Mark III examples produced and was invoiced to W.W. Wallwork Ford of Fargo, North Dakota, before being delivered to its first Los Angeles-area owner via Hi-Performance Motors. By the mid-1970s, the car was purchased by Cobra and GT40 collector Les Lindley, who converted it to semi-competition specification early in its life. In 1975, chassis CSX3243 was leased to Warner Bros. Inc. for use as the hero car of the 1976 comedy film The Gumball Rally , for which it was painted Guardsman Blue. After completion of filming, the car underwent nose repairs and a repaint in dark blue before being returned to Lindley, who retained it in storage for over three decades. After being removed from storage in 2010, it was sold to its next owner and underwent a mechanical refurbishment by McCluskey Ltd. and Maeco Motorsports in California that included the installation of an overhauled 427ci Ford FE V8. The car was subsequently showcased at various events before being purchased eight years ago by the selling dealer, who commissioned a repaint that returned the car to its Gumball Rally appearance. After completion of the work in 2023, the car was displayed as part of the Petersen Automotive Museum’s “Cars of Film &#38; Television” exhibit for approximately two years. Additional features include a four-speed manual transmission, four-wheel disc brakes, staggered-width Halibrand-style wheels, an oil cooler, a hood scoop, rectangular fog lamps with Cibie covers, a CB radio antenna, side-pipe exhaust, and black leather interior upholstery. This 427 Cobra is now offered in Lincolnshire, Illinois, with 1975 documentation from Warner Bros., the car's removed 428ci V8 and other parts, invoices dating back to 2010, a copy of the car's previous title in Les Lindley's name, and a clean Montana title.",
