    "summary": "This 1974 Ferrari Dino 246 GTS is one of approximately 91 US-market spyders built with the “chairs and flares” treatment that included Daytona-style seats as well as flared fenders and 14x7.5” Campagnolo wheels. Specified from the factory in Rosso Chiaro over Nero Connolly leather, chassis 08078 was completed on April 10, 1974, and delivered new to Bill Harrah’s Modern Classic Motors in Reno, Nevada, before being sold to its first owner in Santa Ana, California. The car passed through a series of California owners prior to being relocated to Europe circa 1990. Following time in Switzerland, the Netherlands, and Germany, it was returned to the US in 2022 and purchased by a Canadian collector on BaT in May 2023 . Power is provided by a 2.4-liter quad-cam V6 topped with triple Weber carburetors and paired with a five-speed manual transaxle, and additional equipment includes a chrome grille guard, a black removable targa panel, power windows, air conditioning, and a Sanyo AM/FM radio. Maintenance by Coachwerks Restoration of Victoria, British Columbia, in 2026 is noted to have involved mounting Michelin XWX tires, changing the fuel pump, performing fluid changes, and more as detailed below. This 246 GTS is now offered on dealer consignment in Blaine, Washington, with an owner’s manual in a leather portfolio, a Ferrari Classiche “Red Book,” German-language service invoices, and a Washington State title.",
